  "id": "ex-16-reflexive-verben-a2",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. Echte reflexive Verben are only ever reflexive — sich freuen, sich erinnern, sich beeilen, sich interessieren, sich verlieben always take a reflexive pronoun, with no non-reflexive version. Unechte reflexive Verben go either way with a different meaning: waschen (Ich wasche das Auto — someone else gets washed) vs. sich waschen (Ich wasche mich — I wash myself). The reflexive pronoun itself matches the subject: mich, dich, sich, uns, euch, sich — mostly Akkusativ at this level (Ich freue mich), though a few verbs already take a Dativ reflexive when there's also an Akkusativ object (Ich putze mir die Zähne). Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/16-reflexive-verben-a2",
  "level": "A2",
